{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/518211-on-merit-resonance-shaper","id":518211,"title":"On Merit: Resonance Shaper","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-18T09:40:25-07:00","id":518211,"title":"On Merit: Resonance Shaper","content":"In the text for the Resonance Shaper Merit (WtF2e, p.107), it says that an extended Man+Occult roll can alter the resonance of a locus (at 10 successes per level) or &quot;a small wellspring of Essence&quot; (at five successes per point).<br /> <br /> My question: how is &quot;a small wellspring of Essence&quot; defined? And for that matter, what is the benefit to altering the resonance of an Essence source, outside of making it 'palatable' to different types of spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:01:18-07:00","id":518262,"title":"","content":"I think a small wellspring would just be some place or thing that constantly emits a stream of essence while not forming a locus, perhaps due to said essence being devoured by spirits.<br /> <br /> In regards to the second question, since spirits of a matching resonance can conceal themselves in a locus' zone of influence, you could use it to reveal hidden spirits or give a place to hide for friendly spirits. Also since a zone of influence is always in the 'open' condition, it would keep certain spirits from being able to go through worlds, or let others begin to do so.<br /> <br /> Also there's the general effect essence has on the real world around it. Most notably around loci, if you use the Wellspring rite you can sort of supercharge it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-18-2015, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T07:13:44-07:00","id":521817,"title":"","content":"I took that Merit with my character. My main plan for it was to use it as a negotiation tool when dealing with spirits.<br /> <br /> &quot;How about this: you do what I ask, and I'll see to it that the essence over yonder is resonant with you by week's end&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:57:10-07:00","id":521968,"title":"","content":"Massive events can generate ambient essence which even Uratha can harvest, examples include carnivals (think Rio), raves, sports events, riots, bachelorette parties...<br /> <br /> Guess you can shape those as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}